`litegraph.js` is upstream's `build/litegraph.js` and `litegraph.css` its
`css/litegraph.css`, both at commit
`0555a2f2a3df5d4657593c6d45eb192359888195`, verbatim.

TASKS-foundation.md FND.1 pins that commit. `raw.githubusercontent.com` is not
reachable from the container this was vendored in, so the two files were taken
from the copy the reference repo (`wireon-process-editor`) vendored from
upstream at the same commit, byte for byte. `tools/vendor.sh` fetches them
from upstream on a machine that can reach it and says so if it cannot.

The library is a classic script: it attaches `LiteGraph`, `LGraph`,
`LGraphCanvas` and friends to `window`. Our own code is ES modules and reads
them off `window`; the Flows app loads the script the first time it is opened,
not at page load.

